    "body": "## Description\n\nFix weight-update process group ranks for `xccl` weight updates with\nvLLM internal data parallelism.\n\nFor dense models, vLLM resets each EngineCore's DP rank and size, so\n`get_world_group().rank` does not distinguish internal DP replicas.\nCompute the rank from `data_parallel_index`, the replica world size,\nand the worker rank, then apply the external server offset. This prevents\nduplicate ranks across internal DP replicas while preserving external\nserver offsets.\n\nAdd regression cases covering external server offsets and internal DP\nranks. Mark the tests as requiring vLLM and skip when it is absent.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nNo separate issue.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`)\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (not applicable; no new configuration fields)\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [x] Prepared by a coding agent using the `create-pr` workflow\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n**Breaking Change Details (if applicable):** None.\n\n## Additional Context\n\n- `pre-commit run --all-files`: passed.\n- Conventional Commit message check: passed.\n- The following tests passed: **52 passed, zero skipped**.\n\n  ```bash\n  python -m pytest -q \\\n    tests/test_vllm_worker_rank.py \\\n    tests/test_vllm_moe_reload.py \\\n    tests/test_vllm_pp_mismatch.py \\\n    tests/test_vllm_generation_request.py \\\n    tests/test_select_cpu_tests.py \\\n    tests/test_warmup_process_groups.py\n  ```\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
